      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's completely understandable why clinical solutions might feel inadequate when you're struggling with something this profound. The feeling of an empty core is agonizing, and the thought of stopping the loop can feel like a logical escape from constant pain. If the idea of \"fixing\" feels pointless, perhaps focusing on small moments of sensory experience—like the warmth of a blanket or the taste of water—might offer a momentary anchor to something tangible. Please connect with someone right now; there are people who can listen without trying to \"fix\" the code.",
